 "poem": "183, The Commencement of the Composition Be\nIn his essay on the Archdiocese he\nFought for this by way of proof: \"By decree\nOf Pontifical authority decree\n(As if it had been a free and legislation\nThe Chancellor is stedfast in dedication\nTo that most divine object.\" This translation\nIs by R. B. Eustace Anderson's translation\nOf Voltaire's History publication.\n[Emphasis added by MS.] Translation.\nFrom the Archbishopate to the congregation\nHas been widely disputed situation",
